---
Create a fallible stream of byte chunks from a scoped read handle.

The returned stream borrows the reader and must be consumed inside the `with`
scope that owns the reader.
---
func chunks(reader: FileReader) -> FallibleStream[Bytes, IOError]:
	builtin("blorp_file_chunks_reader_raw")


---
Create a fallible stream of byte chunks with an explicit chunk size.

The returned stream borrows the reader and must be consumed inside the `with`
scope that owns the reader. Passing a non-positive chunk size makes terminal
operations such as `collect_result` return `Err(InvalidInput(...))`.
---
func chunks_with_size(reader: FileReader, chunk_size: Int) -> FallibleStream[Bytes, IOError]:
	builtin("blorp_file_chunks_with_size_reader_raw")


---
Create a fallible stream of text lines from a scoped read handle.

The returned stream borrows the reader and must be consumed inside the `with`
scope that owns the reader. Lines are returned without trailing `\n` or `\r\n`.
---
func lines(reader: FileReader) -> FallibleStream[String, IOError]:
	builtin("blorp_file_lines_reader_raw")


---
Create a fallible stream of individual bytes from a scoped read handle.

The returned stream borrows the reader and must be consumed inside the `with`
scope that owns the reader. Reads are internally buffered; consumers see one
`UInt8` value at a time.
---
func bytes(reader: FileReader) -> FallibleStream[UInt8, IOError]:
	builtin("blorp_file_bytes_reader_raw")


---
Create a fallible stream of sliding byte windows from a scoped read handle.

Each item is an owned `Bytes` value of exactly `size` bytes. If the file is
shorter than `size`, the stream is empty. Passing a non-positive size makes
terminal operations such as `collect_result` return `Err(InvalidInput(...))`.
---
func windows(reader: FileReader, size: Int) -> FallibleStream[Bytes, IOError]:
	builtin("blorp_file_windows_reader_raw")
